  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1234 AM MDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nLooking at Friday and into this weekend, warmer and drier conditions \nare expected to return to the region. Upper ridging will build back \nin over the western CONUS, with very little expected in terms of \nprecipitation. Temperatures will warm a bit as well, with highs \nclimbing into the 70s to possibly low-80s by next week. There will \nstill be chances for isolated convection over the mountains each \nday, but overall not much is expected. With the drier air moving in, \nmay need to monitor for freezing overnight temps in the high \nvalleys, but as of now latest NBM keeps things in the mid to upper-\n30s.",
